--- a/sway-idle/README.md
+++ b/sway-idle/README.md
@@ -7,6 +7,39 @@
 The login remains on tty1; locking uses a separate Linux virtual console and
 authenticates with PAM. Both monitors mirror that console, so password entry
 is shared and only one successful authentication is required.
+
+## DRM monitor power-down — 2026-11-07
+
+The previous console blanking request could succeed while the monitors kept
+their video signal/backlight on. The locker now also sets the active desktop
+connectors' DRM `DPMS` property to `Off`, after securing the lock VT and after
+the compositor releases DRM master. This controls display power through the
+kernel instead of relying on console blanking alone. See the kernel's
+[standard connector properties](https://docs.kernel.org/gpu/drm-kms.html#standard-connector-properties).
+
+The locker keeps DRM master while waiting for the wake key, then restores only
+the connectors it actually powered down, releases every DRM device, and shows
+the existing password prompt. Cleanup also restores saved display state.
+Disconnected, disabled, already powered-off and non-desktop outputs are
+skipped. A master acquisition failure never steals control from a compositor;
+errors are logged and the existing console blanking remains available.
+No privileged process runs compositor IPC or external power commands.
+The 30/60-minute AC policy and 5-minute battery policy are unchanged.
+
+DRM regression checks simulate two monitors, disconnected/disabled/off outputs,
+non-desktop devices, partial power-off and power-on failures, busy DRM master,
+missing resources, repeated calls and cleanup. They never open a real device.
+The physical lock/wake test must also confirm connector power state and the
+return to the existing session. The build additionally links system libdrm;
+headers come from `libdrm-devel` or the existing local Sway build dependencies.
+
+Live validation on 2026-11-07 observed both `HDMI-A-1` and `eDP-1` in DRM
+`Off`, followed by `On` after normal password authentication. Workspaces
+stayed on their original outputs, and the user confirmed both monitors
+physically entered standby. The record is `.build/idle/live-power-validation.json`.
+In that attempt the console had already powered off the connectors before
+the additional DRM request; the fallback itself is covered by the simulated
+failure tests, rather than independently exercised against a failed live blank.
 
